>` key or `no-ticket:\n<non-empty reason>`. Otherwise the writer prints each such line as\n`write-verdict: unfiled residual: <line>` plus one hint line, exits 2,\nand writes nothing. GO and NO-GO alike; CR line endings do not bypass\nit.\n\n**Gate change:** existing judge evidence with unkeyed residual bullets\nis now refused. The rule is documented in\n`docs/handover/verdict-template.md` and\n`docs/handover/judge-brief-template.md` (next to the NO-GO class\nparagraph) so judge briefs carry it.\n\n## Not in this PR (remains for HIMMEL-5843)\n\n- Part 2b: `verdict-go.sh` and the leg wrap check\n(`wrap-subtree-check.sh` / `leg-event.sh`) refuse a WRAPPED message that\nmentions deferred, follow-up or residual without a key.\n- Part 3: the `ice-followups=<n>` tick/board field (edits the held\n`tick.sh`).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- RED first: new cases 22 in `test-write-verdict.sh` failed on main (17\nfailures) before the writer change, pass after.\n- Negative controls: no residual heading unchanged; follow-up prose\nunder `## Evidence` not refused; bullet after the block's blank line not\nrefused; CRLF key-less line refused; empty and whitespace-only CRLF\n`no-ticket:` refused; refusal names the line; verdicts dir listing\nidentical after refusal.\n- Impacted suites green: test-write-verdict, test-verdict-go, test-go,\ntest-grant-round, test-ops-run, test-pr-check-rounds,\ntest-gen-judge-brief, test-brief-lint, test-leg-handoff-threshold-docs.\n\n## Ticket coverage\n\n- Writer refuses unkeyed Non-blocking / Follow-ups / Residual lines (GO\nand NO-GO): done\n- Rule documented in verdict-template.md and judge-brief-template.md:\ndone\n- Part 2b (verdict-go.sh / wrap check refuse unkeyed deferred mentions):\ndeferred → HIMMEL-5843\n- Part 3 (ice-followups tick/board field): deferred → HIMMEL-5843\nleg-burn: calls=22 avg-ctx=79.4k first-turn=54.6k compactions=0\ncost-eq=295.2k profile=leg-impl\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":